  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 305 AM EDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nWnw flow aloft will be temporarily displaced this weekend, as part \nof the western ridge pushes east thru the region, though \ndeamplifying somewhat as it does so. This will turn the upper flow \nmore westerly for a bit, just ahead of a shortwave trof passing late \nin the weekend. Then its back to wnw flow next week.\n\nMostly clear skies out there, though with patchy mid/high clouds \nadvancing from WI and western upper MI. Some fog/stratus also \npopping up, especially in south where surface dew points remain \nhigher than elsewhere. Suppose there is a non-zero of the Lake Huron \nlake breeze kicking off some showers for the ne lower MI coastal \ncounties. Some recent runs of the HRRR/RAP do this, but most \nguidance does not. And some patchy fog returns late tonight. But \notherwise, high pressure passing north of Superior on Friday will \npush drier air into the area. Dew points will lower into the 50s in \nmany areas on Friday, which should make convection more difficult, \neven with a shortwave potentially digging across Lk Huron.\n\nA zone of unsettled wx will remain in the southern lakes/northern OH \nValley for the couple of days. As the surface high heads downstream \nSaturday, and low pressure evolves in the northern plains/southern \nCanada, warmth and moisture will attempt to work north. A decent \nchance for showers and storms should result for late Saturday into \nSunday. Surface cold front goes thru Sunday, and northerly flow and \ncooler/drier air push in Sunday night thru Monday night. Wnw flow \naloft becomes a bit more energetic after that, with shower chances \nresuming Tuesday. Temps area a little cooler, especially Sunday and \nbeyond, but overall pretty yummy late-summer stuff.",
